# EmailJS — delivery for the /contact enquiry form.
#
# Without all three values the form does not pretend to work: it renders a
# visible notice and points the visitor at email and WhatsApp instead. Nothing
# here is secret in the usual sense — Vite inlines VITE_* variables into the
# client bundle, and EmailJS public keys are designed to be exposed. Keep the
# EmailJS account's allowed-origin list restricted to the deployed domain, and
# keep its reCAPTCHA / rate limiting on, because the browser is the only thing
# between these values and the public.
#
# Set the same three in the Vercel project (Settings -> Environment Variables)
# for Production, Preview and Development, then redeploy. A build that does not
# see them ships a form that cannot send.
#
# Values come from the EmailJS dashboard at https://dashboard.emailjs.com
#   Service ID   : Email Services -> the service you connected
#   Template ID  : Email Templates -> the template used for enquiries
#   Access Token : Account -> General -> Public Key
#
# The enquiry template must reference these variables, or the fields arrive
# blank: form_name, from_email, to_name, to_email, project_type, budget, message
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_ACCESS_TOKEN=
